{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>He says</b> — this is what each of the devout, the distant young men, says, for it is known that the body, which is of dust, is a vessel for the supernal soul, which is of the heaven of heavens, and upon separation from the body it returns to its place. Thus it is written: 'and the spirit returns to Elohim who gave it' (Ecclesiastes 12:7), and this is the meaning of 'do not take me up.'" "And the meaning of 'in the generation of generations' — perhaps a spirit from on high will move upon him to help him, so that he does not die in the half of his days; perhaps he will see good."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 102, :notes {0 "Resolved הגוף as 'the body' (not the Gaon); no epithet involved. The phrase 'the distant young men' is hyper-literal; the reference is obscure."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:54.891781879Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}